+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdMwjJ6NYoYjH9na2mo4G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All 70 tests pass, `npm run build` and `npm run lint` are clean.\n\n## What was built\n\nEight services under `src/`, each a factory taking `(bus: EventBus)` and communicating only via events:\n\n| Service | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| `catalog` | CRUD + `product:created`; returns defensive copies |\n| `inventory` | Stock ledger, reserve/release, `inventory:updated` + `inventory:low_stock` |\n| `cart` | Add/remove/update/clear, `cart:updated` on real mutations only |\n| `pricing` | 10% tax, percentage discount codes, price read-model from `product:created` |\n| `orders` | Table-driven state machine (`ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS`), rejects illegal moves |\n| `payment` | Async with `simulateFailure`/`simulateTimeout` options, refunds |\n| `notifications` | Subscriptions, order→user routing from `order:created` |\n| `analytics` | Event counts, revenue, conversion, product leaderboard |\n\nTwo shared, domain-free helpers live in `src/common/` (`id`, `emit`, `money`) — no service imports another service.\n\n## Code review cycle\n\n`/opt/conclave-plugin/conclave` failed with `no agents available (need at least 1 API key)`, so I ran the review with two independent reviewer subagents instead. They converged on real issues, which I fixed and then verified with 12 throwaway regression probes (all passing, probe file removed before commit):\n\n- **Event ordering race (HIGH).** `EventBus.emit` runs only the *first* handler synchronously, so a service registered late gets its `order:created` handler invoked after a subsequent `order:status_changed`. Reversing construction order silently dropped notifications and zeroed revenue. Notifications now buffer events for unknown orders (bounded, oldest-evicted) and flush on introduction; analytics replays unmatched payments the same way.\n- **Revenue double-counting (HIGH).** Duplicate `payment:processed` inflated revenue; duplicate `order:created` inflated the leaderboard and order count. Both are now idempotent per `orderId`.\n- **Payment leaked subscriber failures (MEDIUM).** A throwing `payment:processed` subscriber rejected `processPayment` after the charge was already recorded. Added `emitEventAwaited`, which keeps the ordering guarantee but isolates handler faults.\n- **Money precision (MEDIUM).** Replaced four-point float rounding with integer-cent arithmetic (`src/common/money.ts`), which also makes `subtotal - discount + tax === total` exact. Added input validation to `calculateTotal`, consistent with the other services.\n- **Smaller fixes.** Analytics copies payloads instead of aliasing the publisher's object; ordered carts now count in the conversion denominator; inventory skips no-op emissions; notifications collapsed to a single mailbox map (removing a dead branch).\n\nI deliberately did not act on a few suggestions: emitting non-spec `product:updated`/`product:removed` events (out of spec), adding runtime type guards at all 10 bus-payload cast sites (the bus is internal and `emitEvent` already contains handler faults), and removing the unused `express`/`uuid`/`better-sqlite3` dependencies from the pre-existing scaffold."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":861,"cache_read_input_tokens":100583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":861},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9acea484-8931-43f9-b4f9-99a255b023a5","uuid":"c53d79af-242a-406d-9f04-3527c13e105e","request_id":"req_011CdMwjGztGLMJqpYz1kbaG"}
